  "text": "משכנתılırcerptaThe entry in the $n$th row and $(n-1)$st column can be found using the formula:\n\n$a_{n, n-1} = \\begin{cases} 2^{n-2}-1 & \\text{if } n \\geq 2 \\\\ 0 & \\text{otherwise}\\end{cases}$\n\nThe entry in the $n$th row and $k$th column, for $0 \\leq k \\leq n$, can be found using the formula:\n\n$a_{n, k} = 2^{n-2-k} - 1$.\n\nNow, we need to find the sum of the absolute values of the entries in the $n$th row:\n\n\\begin{align*}\na_n &= \\sum_{k=0}^{n} |a_{n, k}| \\\\\n&= \\sum_{k=0}^{n} |2^{n-k-1} - 1| \\\\\n&= \\sum_{k=0}^{n} (2^{n-k-1} - 1) \\\\\n&= \\sum_{k=0}^{n} 2^{n-k-1} - \\sum_{k=0}^{n} 1 \\\\\n&= \\sum_{k=0}^{n} 2^{n-k-1} - (n+1) \\\\\n&= \\sum_{k=n-1}^{0} 2^{k} - (n+1) \\\\\n&= 2^{n-1} - 2 - (n+1)\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow, we can compute $\\frac{\\log_{10} a_n}{\\log_{10} 2}$:\n\n$\\frac{\\log_{10} a_n}{\\log_{10} 2} = \\frac{\\log_{10} (2^{n-1} - 2 - (n+1))}{\\log_{10} 2} = \\frac{\\log_{10} (2^{n-1} - (n+3))}{\\log_{10} 2} = \\log_2 (2^{n-1} - (n+3))$.\n\nHence, the final answer is $\\log_2 (2^{n-1} - (n+3))$.",
